{
  "schemaVersion": "wod-semantic-glossary-v1",
  "notes": [
    "The semantic lexicon: CrossFit terms that are not movements, and the column each one belongs to.",
    "Built from CrossFit.com (terms explained, the movement library, daily WODs), the Open workout descriptions, and affiliate/box glossaries: Chicago Strength, WODprep, WODhopper, 2POOD, End of Three Fitness, CrossFit iQ, X-treme Athletics, CrossFit Bowmanville, CrossFit First Creek, BoxRox, WODwell, rb100.",
    "columns: format (the workout's format), score (what it is judged by), structure (how the parts are arranged; kept as notes), modifier (a word that qualifies a movement line), load (how a weight or height is written), unit (how a count is written), equipment (what a load belongs to), slang (not part of the workout; dropped from the lines), name (a known benchmark; sets the workout name).",
    "terms are matched case-insensitively on word boundaries; '#' and '×' are matched literally."
  ],
  "format": [
    { "terms": ["amrap", "as many rounds as possible", "as many rounds and reps as possible", "as many reps as possible", "as many calories as possible", "max rounds in", "max reps in"], "value": "amrap", "note": "A countdown of the cap; score is rounds + reps." },
    { "terms": ["for time", "afap", "as fast as possible", "rft", "rounds for time", "chipper", "for time:"], "value": "for_time", "note": "A stopwatch; score is the time. A chipper is for time with many movements done once each." },
